---
title: Markdoc list-syntax tables
---

# Markdoc list-syntax tables

The Markdoc list-syntax table (cells as `*` items, rows separated by `---`)
builds the same table structure as a Markdown pipe table. The first row is the
header unless the table starts with `---`.

## Basic

{% table %}
* Heading 1
* Heading 2
---
* Row 1 Cell 1
* Row 1 Cell 2
---
* Row 2 Cell 1
* Row 2 Cell 2
{% /table %}

## Without a header

{% table %}
---
* foo
* bar
---
* foo
* bar
{% /table %}

## Rich content in cells

Cells are parsed as Markdown, so they can hold code, lists, and paragraphs —
including a `list` tag with a custom marker.

{% table %}
* Foo
* Bar
* Baz
---
*
  ```
  puts "code here"
  ```
*
  {% list type="checkmark" %}
  * Bulleted list in table
  * Second item
  {% /list %}
* Text in a table
{% /table %}

## Column alignment

An `align` annotation on a header cell aligns the whole column; an `align` on
a body cell overrides just that cell.

{% table %}
* Left
* Centre {% align="center" %}
* Right {% align="right" %}
---
* foo
* bar
* baz
---
* longer text
* bar {% align="right" %}
* 1,234
{% /table %}

## Spanning columns

A `colspan` annotation on a cell merges it across columns (no internal rule).

{% table %}
* A
* B
* C
---
* one
* two
* three
---
* spans the first two columns {% colspan=2 %}
* C
{% /table %}

## Spanning rows

A `rowspan` annotation merges a cell down across rows.

{% table %}
* Name
* Detail
---
* Shared across rows {% rowspan=2 %}
* first detail
---
* second detail
{% /table %}
